{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review follow-up for your #9 commit. Same fence and rules as before; new commit on branch 9-gate-lock (no amend), do not push. Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@cursor.com>.\n\nApply:\n1. Add an e2e test: `--tool-idle-ms 300` with the SLOW fake (starts a tool call then goes quiet) ends STALLED with the reason in the record. Record its negative control: temporarily stop passing --tool-idle-ms through to the supervisor, run the test, quote the failure line, restore.\n2. Reject `--tool-idle-ms` values <= 0 (exit 2, reason on stderr).\n3. Replace DefaultHasher in src/lock.rs with a fixed FNV-1a 64-bit hash (a few lines, no crate) so the lock path is stable across builds.\n4. BUSY holder race: if the lock file is empty when read, retry the read briefly (bounded, e.g. 20 × 10ms) before printing.\n5. Doc comment on DELEGATE_IDLE_MS next to DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS: test-only override of the model-idle window.\n6. `ponytail:` comment at settle_dead_supervisor: pid-only liveness, a reused pid hides a dead supervisor; add heartbeat-age check if seen.\n7. Over-engineering hypotheses — apply each ONLY if it removes lines without changing behaviour; otherwise keep the original and say so: (a) status_record.rs:119 rebuild of CliRecord/RunOutput from serde_json::Value → clone prior + set terminal fields; (b) duplicated --tool-idle-ms parsing in run and supervise → one helper; (c) cli.rs local `idle` closure → reuse existing pattern; (d) lock.rs would_block helper → inline matches! at the flock site; (e) tests: assert_ok/stdout_id/run_write → fold into existing Env helpers.\n\nGates: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo test. Report: commit SHA, the negative-control failure line, which hypotheses you applied/kept, test summary. Then Friction (≤3 bullets). STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"b6dfbf0d-2164-45e3-a9e5-f79f7585081e"}
